# loop2 developing itself. First real (non-fake-pi) run of the reviewer/
# verdict mechanism that v0.3 fixed, on a small, genuinely open task.
#
# required=0 removed from the manifest's reviewer step (see below) so the
# verdict is a hard stopping condition — this is specifically what we're
# validating.

LOOP_MAX_ITER=4
LOOP_SESSION=none
LOOP_BRANCH=1
LOOP_BRANCH_BASE=main
LOOP_TEST_CMD=go test ./...
LOOP_WRITER_MODEL=synthetic/hf:zai-org/GLM-5.2
LOOP_REVIEWER_MODEL=anthropic/claude-opus-5
LOOP_FIXER_MODEL=synthetic/hf:zai-org/GLM-5.2

# Anti-cheat. Freeze the tests and this loop's own meta-files so the loop
# cannot pass by editing its own goal or its own gate. Deliberately does NOT
# freeze internal/scaffold/*.go (non-test) — the task may legitimately need
# to change template content or Scaffold() itself.
LOOP_FREEZE='*_test.go loop.env manifest tests.sh writer.md reviewer.md fixer.md'
